onal business times that  she would be quote a thousand percent  interested in participating in a sequel  she went on to say i'd like to think  that maybe they're teachers at sky high  because it's been long enough that they  could go back and teach  there aren't any solid plans for a  sequel so far but the door certainly  remains open  dj daniels had a prolific career as a  child actor he got his start on nbc's in  the house with ll cool j and had a  starring role on the hugelys from  1998-2002  sky high was daniel's first and only  film role his character ethan was part  of a group of sidekicks at the core of  the film and he finds a way to help save  the day despite his seemingly useless  ability to turn himself into a puddle of  goo despite his impressive and hilarious  performance daniel struggled to find  more work as he got older in an extended  2021 interview with vlad tv alongside  his former co-star dl hewgley daniels  opened up about his struggles with  acting fans were shocked to see that  over the years daniels had covered his  face with several tattoos a decision he  claimed to have made partially in  response to his lagging acting career  daniels also talked about how his career  was further derailed when he was  arrested on suspicion of murder in 2012.  it didn't take long for daniels to be  acquitted but the experience left an  impression on him nonetheless nowadays  daniels is pursuing a rap career but he  says that he's always open to returning  to acting  few actors from sky high have kept as  busy as nicolas braun who was just 17  when the film first released  braun told buzzfeed that he was with two  of his friends when he got the call that  he'd landed the role of zach in sky high  and that he couldn't contain his  excitement i screamed and yelled i still  feel that way though when i get apart if  that's the case braun has spent a good  amount of time yelling and screaming  after sky high braun spent a handful of  years bouncing between television shows  before landing a recurring role on 10  things i hate about you from there he  turned his attention to the big screen  for films like the stanford prison  experiment with fellow sky high alum  michael anne garano how to be single and  the perks of being a wallflower  brawn has kept just as busy in recent  years starring in two major films zola  and the big ugly in 2020 alone however  braun truly broke into the mainstream as  fan favorite character cousin greg in  hbo's succession as for what's to come  in bronze still young career you have to  wait and see like everybody else  but it's awesome man it's awesome  who could forget magenta the  shapeshifter that can only become a  guinea pig kelly vitz's character in sky  high had one of the most memorable  powers and definitely the most memorable  hairstyle magenta was put on the  sidekick track with the film's other  protagonists and she helped prove that  anyone no matter their powers has the  ability to be a hero vitz had a  short-lived acting career that began in  2002 when she made a one-line appearance  on the disney channel show lizzie  mcguire her next role was in sky high  and after that she landed roles in the  horror film simon says eye of the  dolphin nancy drew and teenius her final  film role was as ails gilmore in the  2010 film leone  that same year vitz graduated from the  university of california berkeley with a  degree in public health leaving the film  industry to pursue other career goals  steven strait was fresh out of high  school and just 18 years old when he  joined the cast of sky high as the aptly  named warren peace  sky high was straight's first feature  film and only his second professional  acting credit after a guest appearance  on third watch in 2001.  straight followed up the role with the  run of feature films over the next five  years which included the covenant  undiscovered 10 000 bc stop loss and  city island since 2015 straight has  starred in the sci-fi amazon prime  series the expanse as the brave starship  captain jim holden  in a december 2020 interview with geeks  of color strait was asked if he'd ever  consider reprising his role as war and  peace if disney revived sky high in some  way straight said that he's absolutely  open to the idea adding i loved that  experience and they're awesome people  malika hawk started acting in  commercials and tv shows at a young age  by the early 2000s she was used to the  grind of auditions and faceless casting  directors so much that when she and her  twin sister khadijah auditioned for sky  high they didn't even realize it was a  feature film  she told e online we actually thought  the movie was going to go straight to  the disney channel and out of all of  those options we felt so blessed and  overwhelmed to learn that sky high was  going to be our first film huck has  starred in a few more feature films in  the year since sky high most recently  she appeared in the 2016 film definitely  divorcing however hawke is best known  for her recurring role in the reality tv  series keeping up with the kardashians  she's been part of the show since season  2 and she was a main cast member on the  spin-off series dash dolls  khadija hawk mcrae's big break also came  when she was cast in sky high and her  career since has had a similar  trajectory to her sisters as well just  one year later the two went on to star  in the film atl  mccrae's last scripted acting role was  in an episode of kevin hart's real  husbands of hollywood in 2013 but like  her sister she was featured on keeping  up with the kardashians and co-starred  on dash dolls in 2010 she married nfl  defensive end bobby mcrae and in a  january 2021 instagram post the pair  announced a new addition to their family  jake sandvig was only 19 when sky high  arrived in theaters and it marked his  second feature film his first the story  of us starred bruce willis and michelle  pfeiffer and it came out when sandvik  was just 13 years old despite making  appearances in a few tv episodes in the  meantime it was after sky high that his  acting career really started to heat up  sandvik had recurring roles on 20 good  years and cracking up  his next major film role came in 2010's  easy a and a year later he wrote and  starred in the film a bag of hammers  after that sandvik returned to  television moving from weeds to csi to  usa's rush  his most recent roles were in 2017 when  he appeared in bridal boot camp and  hometown hero on the hallmark channel  will harris followed up his role as  speed and sky high with two low budget  features in 2007 on broadway and awaken  the dead after that he spent much of his  time acting in some of the most popular  shows of the decade such as csi friday  night lights and community harris's pace  has never slowed down while continuing  to make guest appearances on a variety  of shows throughout the 2010s he's also  lent his talents to the films in time  and sharon123 he's had a busy 2021 he  made a guest appearance on abc's the  rookie and he took part in the crime  drama no man of god and the horror film  shot in the dark  mary elizabeth winstead who played gwen  in sky high is probably the film's most  recognizable cast member that isn't kurt  russell  though she began her acting career in  1997 sky high was only winstead's third  feature film her role in the film gave  winstead the opportunity to display her  range from kind-hearted classmate to  diabolical villain winstead followed up  sky high with final destination 3 and  horror has been part of her wheelhouse  ever since  she's made appearances in abraham  lincoln vampire hunter and 10  cloverfield lane as well as iconic pop  culture films like scott pilgrim vs the  world and birds of prey winstead's most  recent leading role was as the titular  assassin in the netflix action film kate  while speaking with collider about the  movie winstead took a moment to reflect  on her beloved performance in sky high  and speculated about what role her  character would take in a sequel film  saying  gwen is still operating as a super  villain for sure i went through puberty  twice  for this  kevin heffernan had already starred in  super troopers by the time he got a part  in sky high and he put his comedic  experience to excellent use by bringing  school bus driver ron wilson's unabashed  excitement to life just like the  audience watching sky high ron is an  enthusiastic fan of all things superhero  getting to drive the next generation of  heroes to sky high every morning is a  dream come true for ron and by the end  of the film he gets his own opportunity  to be a hero in the years since sky high  kevin heffernan has continued putting  his talents to work in comedies of all  stripes  he's made guest appearances in some of  the biggest sitcoms of the past two  decades curb your enthusiasm how i met  your mother and veep to name a few and  his film roles which include strange  wilderness and the baby makers have had  a similarly comedic bend currently fans  can catch up with heffernan on truetv's  tacoma fd he created the series with the  help of steve lemmy and the two of them  lead the show as chief terry mcconkey  and captain eddie panisi  as one of the few adults cast and sky  high jim rash already had over a decade  of acting experience under his belt when  he signed on to play mr grayson and his  alter ego stitches  most notably from 2002 through 2006 he  had a recurring role as fenton on that  70s show  though he'd maintained a steady stream  of roles up to that point rash's career  was in many ways just getting started  four years after sky high rash joined  the cast of community as dean craig  pelton a role that he would continue  playing throughout the show's entire six  season run he's also made non-stop  appearances in tv shows and movies for  the past decade most recently he's been  the voice of flicks in star wars  resistance and the riddler in the  animated harley quinn series rash is  also the only member of the sky high  cast to have won an academy award so far  having received the best adapted  screenplay oscar for the descendants in  2012.  dave foley is probably best known for  the work he did before sky high foley  and kevin mcdonald formed sketch comedy  troop the kids in the hall in 1984 and  their tv show of the same name ran from  1988 to 1995. the kids in the hall is  set for a revival in 2022 but foley has  kept himself plenty busy in the years  since it went off the air in addition to  starring in the occasional feature film  foley has spent a majority of his time  making guest appearances on everyone's  favorite tv shows he's taken on live  action series like it's always sunny in  philadelphia and veep as well as  animated shows like robot chicken and  dan vs in 2021 alone foley has made  guest appearances in young sheldon call  your mother superstore and the morning  show there isn't a style of comedy that  foley can't seem to handle perfectly  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite stars are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]

